# Push only to branches Eric owns

NEVER push to a branch, remote, or fork owned by another person or org.

Always assume work is drafted on **Eric's own** PR, branch, and fork (`EricBoittier/...`). Even when the conversation is about someone else's PR (for example `Luthaf:setup-examples` or `metatensor/metatomic#313`), push only to Eric's remote and branch.

If you have been asked to comment on github, be up-front about being an LLM.

In general, do not push unless I have gone through the git-diff and confirmed everything.

## Wait for review before pushing

Do not `git push` until Eric has seen the local diff and explicitly accepted those changes. Preparing a commit locally is fine; pushing is not, even to Eric's fork, even if he earlier said to "do the rerender / update the PR".

Stop after the change is ready, summarize what will go up, and wait.

## conda-smithy rerender

After `conda-smithy rerender`, restore `README.md` (`git restore README.md` or equivalent) and do not stage or commit it. Rerender README churn is not wanted.

Do **not** run plain `conda-smithy rerender` on lammps-metatomic-feedstock (it hangs). Use:

```bash
rerender-feedstock ~/Documents/lammps-metatomic-feedstock
```

That wrapper lives at `~/.local/bin/rerender-feedstock`. It activates the `conda-smithy` env, collapses unused pinning keys, restores README, and does not commit or push. Refuse `~/Documents/metawork/*-feedstock` clones unless `--force` is passed.

```bash
# BAD — commit everything smithy staged, including README.md
git commit -am "MNT: Re-rendered ..."

# GOOD — drop README, then wait for Eric to accept before pushing
git restore --staged README.md
git restore README.md
```

## Never

- `git push` to another user's GitHub namespace (e.g. `Luthaf/metatomic`, `git@github.com:Luthaf/...`)
- Push to upstream org repos (`metatensor/...`) unless Eric explicitly asks in that message
- Push to a branch whose remote tracking user is not Eric, even if Eric has write access
- "Helpfully" update the PR head on someone else's fork
- Push before Eric has accepted the specific local changes
- Include `README.md` in a conda-smithy rerender commit

## Always

- Push to `EricBoittier/<repo>` (or the local `origin` only if it is Eric's fork)
- Create or update Eric's own branch (e.g. `c-api-tutorials-on-313`) and, when asked for a PR, open it from that branch
- Show the diff and wait for a yes before any push

```bash
# BAD — another user's PR head
git push git@github.com:Luthaf/metatomic.git HEAD:setup-examples

# GOOD — Eric's fork and branch
git push git@github.com:EricBoittier/metatomic.git HEAD:c-api-tutorials-on-313
```
